      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s odd that a compile-time check seems to be the way to check for iOS simulator, insead of a runtime check. Do apps always have to be recompiled to run under iOS simulator? I guess that\u0027s different from running iOS apps on Apple Silicon Macs?\n\nAnyway, those questions probably don\u0027t matter. From [here](https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL/issues/11692#issuecomment-2560415330) it sounds like this is a \"hardware\" limitation. If that\u0027s correct (and the iOS simulator exposes this info correctly), it would be more correct to detect this by checking the GPU family with `supportsFeatureSet`. See here for an example:\nhttps://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/metal/PhysicalDeviceMTL.mm;l\u003d411-415;drc\u003d5e7097e945bbe4b35361d83438c6fbbb62748e62",
